  "content": {
    "id": "p30-q4-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "4",
    "prompt": "Find the values of $x$ for which:",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p30-q4a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$(x-1)(x-2)>(x-1)(x-3)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x>1$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}(x-1)(x-2)-(x-1)(x-3)&>0\\\\(x-1)[(x-2)-(x-3)]&>0\\\\x-1&>0\\\\x&>1.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 21
      },
      {
        "id": "p30-q4b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$(x-1)^2(x-2)<(x-1)(x-2)^2$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$1<x<2$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}(x-1)^2(x-2)-(x-1)(x-2)^2&<0\\\\(x-1)(x-2)[(x-1)-(x-2)]&<0\\\\(x-1)(x-2)&<0.\\end{align*}$$\nThe upward-opening graph is below the axis between its zeroes. Hence $1<x<2$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 28
      },
      {
        "id": "p30-q4c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$(x-2)^2(x-3)^3\\ge(x-2)^3(x-3)^2$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=2$ or $x=3$.\n\nThe difference is the negative of a product of squares.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}(x-2)^2(x-3)^3-(x-2)^3(x-3)^2&\\ge0\\\\(x-2)^2(x-3)^2[(x-3)-(x-2)]&\\ge0\\\\-(x-2)^2(x-3)^2&\\ge0.\\end{align*}$$\nThe left-hand side is non-positive, so the inequality holds only when it is zero. Hence $x=2$ or $x=3$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 35
      },
      {
        "id": "p30-q4d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$(x-1)^2(x-2)^2\\ge(x-1)^2(x+2)^2$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x\\le0$ or $x=1$.\n\nRetain $x=1$, where the common squared factor is zero.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}(x-1)^2(x-2)^2-(x-1)^2(x+2)^2&\\ge0\\\\(x-1)^2[(x-2)^2-(x+2)^2]&\\ge0\\\\-8x(x-1)^2&\\ge0.\\end{align*}$$\nFor $x\\ne1$, the square is positive, so the product is non-negative when $x\\le0$. At $x=1$ the product is zero. Hence $x\\le0$ or $x=1$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 35
      }
    ]
  },
